{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779114271,"nonce":"u7ILBdpVKT2q+94QBuDT05WivQs=","title":"Phase 5c: make Studio shell stage-aware and persist provenance drafts","message":"## Parent / coordination\n- Roadmap: `fa3978f` — Feedbax/Mandible MVP integration roadmap, Phase 5.\n- Pipeline spec: `0c46f69`.\n- Structural authoring spec: `5378a5d`.\n- State-owner slice: `e530093`.\n- Collection/provenance slice: `4e0d925`.\n\n## Problem\nAfter the workspace state-owner and collection slices, the visible Studio shell still needs to stop presenting the app as a graph editor plus unrelated bottom tabs. Phase 5's product boundary is that the top and bottom panes are coordinated views over the selected pipeline stage, with autosaved draft/spec/provenance state and no hidden panel-local executable meaning.\n\n## Scope\nMake the Studio shell stage-aware and persist the draft/provenance state needed for the intended product model:\n\n- Add stage-aware navigation/selection affordances that drive both top and bottom panes from `StudioWorkspaceSpec` state.\n- Route training, eval, analysis, and report panels through active stage/scenario/collection state rather than independent tab-local ownership.\n- Persist active stage, stage UI state, draft versions, validation/execution status, and executed snapshot refs through autosave/project save.\n- Surface pipeline provenance and collection outputs in the lower workspace so the user can inspect stage inputs, outputs, manifests, artifacts, and exact executed snapshots.\n- Keep the implementation ready for richer Phase 6 visual objective/biomechanics/report UX without adding compatibility-only ownership shims.\n\n## Non-goals\n- No polished visual objective authoring layer in this slice.\n- No Mandible UI or provider-action UX.\n- No full live cloud runner UX.\n- Do not preserve old tab/global-store semantics when they conflict with stage-owned state.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- Selecting a stage changes the active stage in `workspaceStore` and the top/bottom panes render stage-appropriate authoring/workspace views.\n- Autosave/project save reopens with active stage, draft scenario/spec state, stage collections, status, manifests/artifacts, and executed snapshot refs intact.\n- The lower workspace shows inspectable provenance for stage inputs/outputs/manifests/artifacts without relying on one global run selection.\n- Tests or focused component/store coverage prove stage selection and persisted workspace draft/provenance state survive round trips.\n\n---\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}